<title>SOUTH KOREA: Seoul bourse watchdog seeks international ties.</title>
<headline>Seoul bourse watchdog seeks international ties.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-06-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Securities Supervisory Board said on Tuesday it planned to sign a memorandum of understanding with its major foreign counterparts to expand international cooperation.</p>
<p>The board said in a statement it planned to form ties with its counterparts in Britain, Hong Kong and other countries on expanding exchanges of information.</p>
<p>It said such ties were needed in line with the increasing internationalisation of stock markets in major countries.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
